  {
    "pkattachmentId": 57774,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 63,
    "fileId": 27736,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Pleomorphic adenoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Classic marked hyperintensity (similar intensity to cerebrospinal fluid) on a T2-weighted fat-suppressed protocol. This right retropharyngeal mass shows connection to the deep lobe of the parotid gland.",
    "source": "Lester D.R. Thompson",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/27736.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/thumb_27736.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 57775,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 63,
    "fileId": 27737,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Pleomorphic adenoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The classic histological features are seen, with a chondromyxoid matrix blending imperceptibly with the myoepithelial cells and showing small ducts in the background.",
    "source": "Lester D.R. Thompson",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/27737.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/thumb_27737.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 57776,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 63,
    "fileId": 27738,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Pleomorphic adenoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The imperceptible blending of the components of pleomorphic adenoma are an aid to diagnosis. Small ducts are seen, surrounded by myoepithelial cells that merge into the adjacent chondromyxoid matrix.",
    "source": "Lester D.R. Thompson",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/27738.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/thumb_27738.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 57777,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 63,
    "fileId": 27740,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Pleomorphic adenoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Clinically recurrent tumours demonstrate numerous nodules of pleomorphic adenoma set within fibrous connective tissue and fat. The cellularity is variable. There is no destructive infiltration and there is a lack of pleomorphism.",
    "source": "Lester D.R. Thompson",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/27740.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/thumb_27740.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 57778,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 63,
    "fileId": 27741,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Pleomorphic adenoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Many tumours are sampled by core needle biopsy. When all of the elements are present, a diagnosis can be made, while recognizing the sampling limitations.",
    "source": "Lester D.R. Thompson",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/27741.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/thumb_27741.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 57779,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 63,
    "fileId": 27742,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Pleomorphic adenoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "High-power view of the core needle sample demonstrates the characteristic features of pleomorphic adenoma.",
    "source": "Lester D.R. Thompson",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/27742.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/thumb_27742.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 57780,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 63,
    "fileId": 27744,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Pleomorphic adenoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Tumours show remarkable variation in appearance, with a prominent spindled cell myoepithelial component illustrated. Focal squamous metaplasia is present.",
    "source": "Lester D.R. Thompson",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/27744.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/thumb_27744.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 57781,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 63,
    "fileId": 27745,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Pleomorphic adenoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Calcification and even bone formation may be seen in pleomorphic adenoma, often in those present for a long clinical duration.",
    "source": "Lester D.R. Thompson",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/63/27745.jpg",
